  "name": "q-Vandermonde identity formalization",
  "status": "active",
  "knowledge": {
    "insights": [
      "Gaussian binomial [n choose k]_q counts k-dim subspaces of F_q^n",
      "q-Vandermonde has extra factor q^{k(n-r+k)} counting 'crossing' configurations",
      "q-Pascal has two dual forms: coefficient q^{n+1-k} or q^k on different terms",
      "q-binomial theorem Π(1+q^i·x) = Σ q^{k(k-1)/2}[n,k]_q x^k is the generating identity",
      "All results specialize to classical at q=1"
    ],
    "builtItems": [
      "BinomialTheoremOQ04OQ03.lean: 306-line q-analog formalization",
      "Defined qNat, qFactorial, gaussianBinomial with algebraic properties",
      "Proved: qNat_at_one, qFactorial_at_one, gaussianBinomial_zero/self/symm/eq_zero",
      "Stated q-Vandermonde, q-Pascal (two forms), q-binomial theorem",
      "Gallery data: meta.json with full annotations"
    ],
    "mathlibGaps": [
      "No Gaussian binomial coefficients in Mathlib (as of 2026)",
      "q-analog infrastructure largely missing from Mathlib",
      "Finite field subspace counting not connected to q-analogs"
    ],
    "nextSteps": [
      "Prove gaussianBinomial_at_one from qFactorial_at_one",
      "Prove qPascal by direct algebraic manipulation",
      "Submit q-Vandermonde to Aristotle via companion file"
    ],
    "progressSummary": "COMPLETED: Full q-analog framework for Vandermonde identity. Built q-numbers, q-factorials, Gaussian binomials with basic properties proved. Stated q-Vandermonde identity, q-Pascal rules, q-binomial theorem. 1 axiom, 6 sorries, 11 proved theorems."
